{"kind":"request","text":"BO1: the fragment and the commons. First slice of the boundary-objects design note (notes/2026-10-28-boundary-objects-in-use.md, section 9, landed 25930f62), child of request bc4aa093. Replaces f34cec9f, which described the note's first version. Kernel filing gate applies.\n\nScope, as the note's slice list states it:\n1. A fragment on references in packages/contract/src/definition.ts: a reference to a retained document or to an entry may carry a fragment string; the record stores it and checks nothing; the media type of the referenced thing defines its meaning (RFC 3986; Media Fragments t and xywh, RFC 8118 page, RFC 7111 row). The capture and retained-files references carry it.\n2. platform:commons@1 with one act, note: text, a detached text with a media type, at most 64 KiB; about, a list of references with optional fragments, to documents and entries in any room the signer reads, bounded by entry size. No guards, no effects. Grant commons.write to every member role at room creation; membership can narrow it. commons joins PlatformDefinition in packages/contract/src/scope.ts. Pinned in the newest creation cohort (scope/src/creation-versions.ts) and in platform/src/native-catalog.ts (80 to 81 versions; the Workers' PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS do not change).\n3. A package that declares the commons endpoint is refused at install in a room without the commons, with commons-missing.\n4. The generic interface shows a room's notes as a thread and as a table over notes whose text is data, each with its author.\n5. docs/use-cases.md in the same head: link the note, and reword \"Pointing at things, and claims of agreement\" as a reading, a mark and an agreement as notes. Say what case 50 leaves out, and that group 3's rooms are each party's own room shared with the authority (approval 1703cf3b points).\n6. Witness W1 (the bill table), in a new room on the hosted platform: fourteen row notes about pages of two documents, one list note, four marks, the question retained and a note about it and the four rows; every act recorded with its signer; the table view shows the rows with their pages; a view of either document lists the rows, the marks and the question with their authors; nothing of the member's attributed to the agent.\n\nNot in this slice: views as notes (BO2), the install screen's slot list and the snag list (BO3), the matter view (BO4), views as code (BO5).","body":{"conditions":"Review cites docs/kernel.md section 7 (fragment on references, commons platform part, catalog 80 to 81); commons-missing refusal by name; docs/use-cases.md links the note and rewords pointing and agreement as notes; witness W1 recorded in a new hosted room with immutable evidence; the note's What changes where rows this slice closes are updated; gate green.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}